WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.639
NCIS: Los Angeles has dropped a bombshell:
Renée Felice Smith's Nell Jones is planning

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:10.320
to leave, potentially for good, at the end
of the show's eleventh season.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.509
But what's the real reason Nell will no longer
be a part of the show?

00:00:14.509 --> 00:00:19.000
On the episode entitled "Fortune Favors the
Brave," Nell's reason for wanting to leave

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.410
is revealed: the job has changed her so much
that she even struggles to get out of bed

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.140
in the mornings to come to work.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.290
She confessed as much to Kensi Blye early
on in the episode.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:35.070
"I don't think I want to be an agent anymore."

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.070
"Okay…

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.070
Um…"

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.399
Kensi tried to suggest that Nell rather stick
to her old base of Ops rather than going out

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:45.409
into the field as an agent, but that wasn't
the solution Nell was looking for either.

00:00:45.409 --> 00:00:49.600
"Kens, I'm going to resign from NCIS."

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.800
Though Kensi suggested a holiday and was supportive
of Nell's confliction and struggles, she was

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.889
somewhat less supportive of her desire to
resign from the team.

00:00:59.889 --> 00:01:04.930
To be fair, the job Nell wants to leave behind
is a tough one, with plenty of grief and stress

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:15.250
involved.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:19.111
Between that and the personal troubles Nell
has endured with her mother's illness, it's

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:23.460
completely understandable that she's having
serious doubts about her job right now.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:28.300
Nell was previously touted to be taking over
from Operations Manager Hetty Lang, who has

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.880
also been fairly absent on NCIS: Los Angeles
recently.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.140
She seemed like she'd be the perfect fit for
the job.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:39.299
But just a few episodes ago, Nell's future
on the series suddenly became unclear.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.560
Instead of pushing to keep Nell in the fold,
Hetty indicated that she was instead now looking

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.979
at Callen to take over for her when the time
comes.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:51.750
Hetty being Hetty, it seems she was well aware
that Nell's inner turmoil would probably lead

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.219
her to walk away from the job opportunity.

00:01:55.219 --> 00:01:58.729
"Now… begone."

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:04.810
The episode closed with Nell finally telling
Hetty that she was resigning, but the ever-stoic

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.229
operations manager gives her another option
before she makes her final decision.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:13.400
In Hetty's view, Nell is free to leave if
she wants but first, she's going to have to

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.920
burn through a few weeks' worth of unused
vacation days.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:26.230
" If I don't hear from you once they've elapsed,
you can consider yourself resigned."

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:30.769
That unused vacation time indicates that Nell
may well be suffering from a serious case

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:32.010
of burnout.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:36.170
Between working as hard as she does and spending
time at her sick mother's bedside, Nell's

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:41.000
head is likely spinning too fast in every
possible direction, which could easily be

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.120
the cause of her high stress levels and lack
of desire to go to work.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.709
When Nell walked away to tell Eric about her
decision, she stopped for a moment to look

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:52.739
around the office, seemingly saying goodbye
to the place that had been a second home to

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.240
her for almost a decade.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.439
Her relationship with Eric also seems to have
suffered lately, with the pair appearing to

00:02:58.439 --> 00:02:59.439
have communication issues.

00:02:59.439 --> 00:03:05.580
A relationship between Eric and Nell was long
hoped for by NCIS: LA fans, who noticed their

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.129
flirtations early on and hoped to see them
seal the deal.

00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:13.270
It looked like their relationship was finally
confirmed, but season 11 has brought them

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.349
some unexpected troubles.

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:20.400
Episode 19 saw Nell desperately trying to
avoid talking to Eric at every turn something

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.049
that's not usually a good sign in a relationship
when major decisions are being made.

00:03:25.049 --> 00:03:27.769
"I are you avoiding me?"

00:03:27.769 --> 00:03:32.550
And even though there have been hints of Eric
also waving goodbye to NCIS, the turmoil between

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:36.019
him and Nell might instead see the couple
split.

00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:40.390
Actor Barrett Foa's time away from the show
during the early episodes of season 11 were

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:43.470
to allow the actor time to appear in a play.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:48.280
His return to the small screen and the Ops
center has seemed to be fairly permanent despite

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:53.830
him previously looking for jobs in San Francisco,
where Nell's mother is being treated.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.950
Nell isn’t in the preview for Season 11’s
20th episode, but the why of it all still

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:57.950
remains to be seen.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:01.269
If she has decided to leave, will fans get
a chance to see her again?

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:03.610
Or has she already disappeared for good?

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:08.360
Like many other TV shows have had to do recently,
NCIS: LA has had to cut production on the

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.000
current season short.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Instead of the usual 24 episodes of season
11, fans will only get 21.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.750
This could mean that the uncertainty around
Nell's decision may be dragged out even longer

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:23.190
than originally planned if her vacation days
haven't elapsed by the time the truncated

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.789
season reaches its end.

00:04:24.789 --> 00:04:29.690
So far, Renée Felice Smith hasn't yet made
an official announcement about leaving the

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:34.400
show, but a recent Instagram post of hers
directed fans to tune in to see a "wistful"

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.720
Nell on Sunday night.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.930
The studio also hasn't confirmed that she's
definitely departing the team, leaving fans

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:43.650
with no option but to keep on watching to
see where Nell ends up.

